{%- comment -%}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRUCTURED DATA (custom vcollect)

Custom (not Impact): the site-wide entity graph. Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid, on every page.

Why this snippet exists next to 'microdata-schema':
  - 'microdata-schema' describes the *resource* of the page (Product, ItemList, BlogPosting). It stays the owner of
    that markup, comments and verified values included.
  - this snippet describes the *publisher* (Organization) and the *site* (WebSite), plus the page-level wrapper for
    collections and pages. Those nodes used to live inside 'microdata-schema' but were emitted on the homepage only,
    so every other URL of the store told search engines nothing about who publishes it.

Everything is emitted as a single @graph with stable @id values, so the nodes reference each other instead of repeating
themselves. That is what makes the store read as one entity rather than one anonymous page per URL.

No value is hardcoded here. Editorial facts come from the "Entity and SEO" theme settings, contact and postal identity
from the shop resource. Every key is conditioned: an empty setting emits no key rather than an empty string.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign organization_id = shop.url | append: '#organization'
  assign website_id = shop.url | append: '#website'
  assign webpage_id = canonical_url | append: '#webpage'

  comment
    The logo is the admin brand asset first (Settings > Brand), falling back to the theme's sharing image so the key
    survives whichever of the two the merchant maintains. `image` prefers the 1200 x 630 sharing image, which is the
    landscape visual meant to be shown next to a citation.
  endcomment
  assign entity_logo = shop.brand.logo | default: settings.social_sharing_image
  assign entity_image = settings.social_sharing_image | default: shop.brand.logo
  assign entity_description = shop.brand.short_description | default: shop.description
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  sameAs is read from the theme's own social settings, because those are exactly what the footer icons render: the
  markup can never claim a profile the site does not link. Every social setting is scanned, so a profile added later in
  the theme editor joins the list by itself. The "Additional profile URLs" setting covers the channels the theme has no
  field for (Whatnot and friends).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign same_as = ''
  assign social_setting_ids = 'social_facebook,social_twitter,social_threads,social_pinterest,social_instagram,social_vimeo,social_whatsapp,social_tumblr,social_youtube,social_tiktok,social_linkedin,social_snapchat,social_fancy,social_wechat,social_reddit,social_line,social_spotify,social_21buttons' | split: ','

  for setting_id in social_setting_ids
    assign social_url = settings[setting_id]
    if social_url != blank
      assign same_as = same_as | append: social_url | append: '|'
    endif
  endfor

  if settings.entity_same_as != blank
    assign extra_profiles = settings.entity_same_as | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
    for extra_profile in extra_profiles
      assign extra_profile = extra_profile | strip
      if extra_profile != blank
        assign same_as = same_as | append: extra_profile | append: '|'
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign same_as = same_as | split: '|'
-%}

{%- comment -%} Node 1: the publisher. Every other node points back at this @id. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture organization_node -%}
  {
    "@type": "OnlineStore",
    "@id": {{ organization_id | json }},
    "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
    {%- if settings.entity_alternate_name != blank -%}
      "alternateName": {{ settings.entity_alternate_name | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_legal_name != blank -%}
      "legalName": {{ settings.entity_legal_name | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_founding_date != blank -%}
      "foundingDate": {{ settings.entity_founding_date | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Legal identifiers. SIREN identifies the company, SIRET the establishment, and the VAT number is the one a buyer
      or a marketplace can check against the EU VIES register. Together they are what makes the entity verifiable by a
      third party rather than merely self-declared, which is the whole point of publishing them.

      All three were carried over from the JSON-LD that used to live inside the "À propos" page body, itself checked
      against the company register on 30/07/2026. That block was removed once these keys existed here, so the facts
      are now published from a single place.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_siren != blank -%}
      "identifier": {
        "@type": "PropertyValue",
        "name": "SIREN",
        "value": {{ settings.entity_siren | json }}
      },
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_siret != blank -%}
      "taxID": {{ settings.entity_siret | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_vat_id != blank -%}
      "vatID": {{ settings.entity_vat_id | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_telephone != blank -%}
      "telephone": {{ settings.entity_telephone | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_founder != blank -%}
      "founder": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": {{ settings.entity_founder | json }}
      },
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if entity_logo != blank -%}
      "logo": {{ entity_logo | image_url: width: entity_logo.width | prepend: 'https:' | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if entity_image != blank -%}
      "image": {{ entity_image | image_url: width: entity_image.width | prepend: 'https:' | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if entity_description != blank -%}
      "description": {{ entity_description | strip_html | strip | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if shop.brand.slogan != blank -%}
      "slogan": {{ shop.brand.slogan | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.entity_price_range != blank -%}
      "priceRange": {{ settings.entity_price_range | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if shop.email != blank -%}
      "email": {{ shop.email | json }},
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if shop.address.address1 != blank or shop.address.city != blank -%}
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        {%- if shop.address.address1 != blank -%}
          "streetAddress": {{ shop.address.address1 | json }},
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if shop.address.city != blank -%}
          "addressLocality": {{ shop.address.city | json }},
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if shop.address.province != blank -%}
          "addressRegion": {{ shop.address.province | json }},
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if shop.address.zip != blank -%}
          "postalCode": {{ shop.address.zip | json }},
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Deliberately the last key and the only unconditional one, so the object always closes without a trailing
          comma whichever of the optional keys above are present. It is safe to make it unconditional: a Shopify store
          always has a country in Settings > General, it is required to create the store.

          country_code is the ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 form schema.org expects, verified against
          shopify.dev/docs/api/liquid/objects/address on 30/07/2026.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        "addressCountry": {{ shop.address.country_code | json }}
      },
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if same_as.size > 0 -%}
      "sameAs": [
        {%- for profile_url in same_as -%}
          {{ profile_url | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ],
    {%- endif -%}
    "url": {{ shop.url | json }}
  }
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Node 2: the site, with the search action that powers a sitelinks search box.

  The search target is built with `assign` rather than inline in the output tag below. That is not a style choice: the
  template contains a literal `{search_term_string}` placeholder, and Liquid's parser fails on the braces when they sit
  inside an output tag ("Liquid syntax error: Variable is not terminated", raised by Shopify on push). Assigning first
  keeps the braces out of the expression being parsed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign search_target = request.origin | append: routes.search_url | append: '?q={search_term_string}'
-%}
{%- capture website_node -%}
  {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    "@id": {{ website_id | json }},
    "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
    "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
    "inLanguage": {{ request.locale.iso_code | json }},
    "publisher": { "@id": {{ organization_id | json }} },
    "potentialAction": {
      "@type": "SearchAction",
      "target": {
        "@type": "EntryPoint",
        "urlTemplate": {{ search_target | json }}
      },
      "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
    }
  }
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Node 3: the page wrapper, for the page types no other snippet describes.

  Products and articles are deliberately excluded: 'microdata-schema' already emits a Product and a BlogPosting for
  them, and wrapping those in a second page-level node adds nothing while risking a conflicting statement.

  On pages, Shopify's Liquid `page` object exposes `published_at` but no `updated_at` (verified against
  shopify.dev/docs/api/liquid/objects/page, 30/07/2026), so dateModified has to come from a metafield. Freshness is a
  selection criterion for generative engines, so an absent date is better than a frozen one: the key is only emitted
  when the metafield really holds a value.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign page_node_type = ''

  case request.page_type
    when 'collection'
      if collection != blank
        assign page_node_type = 'CollectionPage'
        assign page_node_name = collection.title
        assign page_node_description = collection.description | strip_html | strip
      endif
    when 'page'
      comment
        The "À propos" page is the entity page: it gets AboutPage and is linked to the Organization by mainEntity.
        Skipped when the page body already carries its own AboutPage block (the version published in the page content
        before this snippet existed), so the two can never compete.
      endcomment
      unless page.content contains 'AboutPage'
        comment
          The entity page is recognised by its handle, not by its template. Tying it to the template suffix looked
          tidier but was wrong in practice: the page kept rendering through the default page template, so it was typed
          WebPage and lost its link to the Organization. What makes a page the entity page is which page it is, not
          which template happens to render it.
        endcomment
        if page.handle == settings.entity_about_page_handle and settings.entity_about_page_handle != blank
          assign page_node_type = 'AboutPage'
        else
          assign page_node_type = 'WebPage'
        endif
        assign page_node_name = page.title
        assign page_node_description = page.content | strip_html | truncatewords: 40
      endunless
      assign page_date_published = page.published_at
      assign page_date_modified = page.metafields.vcollect.date_maj.value
  endcase
-%}

{%- capture page_node -%}
  {%- if page_node_type != blank -%}
    {
      "@type": {{ page_node_type | json }},
      "@id": {{ webpage_id | json }},
      "url": {{ canonical_url | json }},
      "name": {{ page_node_name | json }},
      {%- if page_node_description != blank -%}
        "description": {{ page_node_description | json }},
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if page_date_published != blank -%}
        "datePublished": {{ page_date_published | date: '%Y-%m-%d' | json }},
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if page_date_modified != blank -%}
        "dateModified": {{ page_date_modified | date: '%Y-%m-%d' | json }},
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if page_node_type == 'AboutPage' -%}
        "mainEntity": { "@id": {{ organization_id | json }} },
      {%- endif -%}
      "inLanguage": {{ request.locale.iso_code | json }},
      "isPartOf": { "@id": {{ website_id | json }} },
      "publisher": { "@id": {{ organization_id | json }} }
    }
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Assembled through a delimited list so the separating commas are driven by forloop rather than written by hand: a node
  that turns out empty drops out without leaving an orphan comma behind.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign graph_nodes = ''
  assign graph_nodes = graph_nodes | append: organization_node | append: '@@node@@'
  assign graph_nodes = graph_nodes | append: website_node | append: '@@node@@'

  assign trimmed_page_node = page_node | strip
  if trimmed_page_node != blank
    assign graph_nodes = graph_nodes | append: trimmed_page_node | append: '@@node@@'
  endif

  assign graph_nodes = graph_nodes | split: '@@node@@'
-%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {%- for graph_node in graph_nodes -%}
      {{ graph_node }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
